WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.110
- This is Joanna.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.963
She thinks she has COVID 19,

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.763
and now she has a nostril
so we can test her.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.470
But this isn't just any nose swab.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.340
It's part of a high-tech PCR-like test

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.040
called the Cue Health Monitoring System.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.690
And you can do it all at home,

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.830
no standing in line at the testing center,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.060
and then waiting a few
days to get the result.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.010
See, first you insert this cartridge

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.760
into this cartridge reader.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.130
Then after you've
snotted-up this fancy swab,

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.940
it gets inserted into the cartridge,

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.680
which then sends the result to your phone,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.950
and confirmed positive.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.510
Definitely did not want to
be in the same room as her,

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:40.940
but I am the real Joanna.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.660
And I recently did have COVID

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.870
and I really have been
testing two new advanced

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.870
at-home molecular tests on myself.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.810
Number one, the Cue Reader
and Cue COVID 19 Test,

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:57.280
which together start at $474.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.740
Number two, the Detect COVID Test;

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.740
the starter kit starts at $75.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.700
Clearly, these are not
your twentysomething,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.180
a pair box of at-home rapid antigen tests.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.060
Instead, these are at home molecular tests

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.360
that work like PCR tests.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.410
So, do you really need one of these?

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.590
And if you do, which one do you get?

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.030
We're going to get to all of that,

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.530
but first you really need
to understand the difference

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.170
between these tests and
those inexpensive tests.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.610
Don't worry, she's going
to help with it all.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.010
She's far more capable than me.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.769
Okay, first, the at-home
antigen tests like these,

00:01:32.769 --> 00:01:35.870
which have been available
and at times hard to find

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.420
over the past few months.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.690
Swab the nose, then play six drops here,

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.990
and then stick the swab in here.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.400
Here's what's happening,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.740
those drops of liquid help
push the sample to the paper,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.820
and the paper itself is
loaded up with antibodies

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.490
that detect an antigen or a viral protein.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.740
If detected, it will be positive.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.520
if not negative.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.510
These tests, which take up to 15 minutes

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.590
to return results,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.350
may not detect COVID-19

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.460
in the early stages of infection,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.760
but they tend to detect it,

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.940
when you're carrying a lot of the virus.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.800
On the other hand,

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.880
a molecular test is more sensitive

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.010
and can detect COVID earlier.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.210
These tests use chemicals and equipment

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.860
to amplify a sample's genetic material,

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.320
billions of times to
spot traces of the virus.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.400
And now we do that all from your home.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.410
Let's try the Detect system
to illustrate what's happening

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.870
during a molecular test.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.393
And back to swabbing;

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.750
after that you insert the
swab into this test tube

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.763
and stir for 15 seconds.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:40.040
Then you open this pouch
and get out this cap

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.010
and screw it on the tube.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.610
The cap has a little enzyme

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.570
that helps with the process
of amplifying your sample.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:47.790
You shake it up real well

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.950
so it all gets mixed up together.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.170
Then you place it in the Detect Hub

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.470
for about 55 minutes.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.303
The Detect App,

00:02:56.303 --> 00:02:58.600
which thankfully provides
a step-by-step guide

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.433
to all this,

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:02.120
will alert you when it's
ready to be taken out.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.600
Oh, and we're not done;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.260
Then you open another pack
and squeeze the liquid

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.710
from this dropper into this reader,

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.640
then you place your test tube
in the chimney of the reader.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.710
Then, finally, the sample
pours into the reader.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.900
Then, you wait another 10 minutes.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.900
And then finally, one line
negative, two lines positive.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.670
The Cue Test does pretty
much the same thing

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.400
without you having to
pretend you're some sort

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.210
of mad scientist.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.540
You put the Cue cartridge into the reader,

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.620
then you put the fancy swab in your nose,

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.380
and collect the sample.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.340
Then you insert the
swab into the cartridge;

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.240
inside it mixes with
liquid and some enzymes

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.000
and then it does its thing
for about 20 minutes.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.450
The reader also connects to
your phone via Bluetooth.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.440
When the test is done, boom,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:51.280
your results pop up right
in the Cue Health App.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.450
So molecular tests can detect
your COVID infection earlier,

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.920
than antigen tests.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.680
But how much earlier?

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.340
experts told me it could be anywhere

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.360
from six hours to two days.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.570
And it depends on a couple of factors,

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.170
including the variant.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.840
And that's pretty much how it went for me.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.073
On Friday, I started to feel symptoms.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.150
A rapid antigen test said negative.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.530
The Detect test positive.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.350
A PCR test taking the next morning

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.940
at a lab confirmed positive as well.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.963
By Sunday, the rapid
antigen tests said positive.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.470
Both Detect and Cue report

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.910
that they are around 97% accurate

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.090
as a laboratory PCR test.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.810
I called up Dr. Michael Mina,

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.560
an epidemiologist and COVID testing expert

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.240
to ask him more about these
tests and if we can trust them.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.323
He previously served as
an adviser to Detect.

00:04:42.323 --> 00:04:44.760
- I can certainly trust the readout.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.760
The tools are working very well.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.170
It's not a new technology.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:51.660
It's just a new packaging
of a known technology,

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.570
and it's really sort of
taking what only lived

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.210
in big instruments

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.560
and putting it into very
simple little boxes.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.670
- So which one is better?
Well, I love the Cue.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.310
It's basically a little
COVID testing computer,

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.630
but it also costs as much as a computer.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.910
The reader is $249 and a
pack of three tests is $225.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.140
You can buy it on cuehealth.com.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:18.290
The NBA, MLB, Netflix
and Google are just a few

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.570
using the system.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.040
Eventually, Cue wants to
sell other types of tests,

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.680
including flu that you'd take

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.500
and then plug into the cartridge reader.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.470
While the detect requires more steps

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.420
and takes longer to process the result,

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.720
It's more affordable
which is why I bought it.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:35.850
The starter kit is $75 and
includes the Hub and one test;

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.130
extra tests cost $49,

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.900
but the company plans to
bring that price down soon.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.840
You can buy it on detect.com,

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.490
if they have stock.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.400
The site often says exactly what day

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.430
and time there'll be more stock in,

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.690
but supplies go very quickly.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.860
Detect is also working on a future test

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.910
that will test for COVID and flu.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.410
There's another $75 molecular test

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.290
called the Lucira Check It.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.040
But it is a single use test,

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.310
and I didn't try it while I had COVID.

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:04.920
And it's really those higher prices

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.510
that hold back these tests

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.260
from being as useful as the antigen tests,

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:10.310
experts told me.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.300
Plus, you're going to
want those antigen tests

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.780
as the virus progresses,

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:15.680
and you want to get out of quarantine.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.700
- If you're trying to use
the test to ask the question,

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.230
can I exit isolation and go back to work

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.630
or be around my family safely,

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.800
a rapid antigen test is the test to use

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.510
that will give you that information.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.310
- We just got the results.
We're both COVID free.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:34.240
Molecular tests are so sensitive,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.690
they can show positive results

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:39.180
even after the virus is no
longer alive in your body.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.950
But Hey, the idea of having
a gadget in your house

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:44.890
that saves you a trip to
the doctor is the dream.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:45.723
For now though,

00:06:45.723 --> 00:06:47.500
you need to be willing to pay way more

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.350
than those antigen tests.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:53.663
Luckily, fiberglass Joanna
is super duper rich, oops.

00:06:55.595 --> 00:06:58.512
(orchestral music)

